@startuml usecase
title COLORS Web Application - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

actor "User" as User
actor "MySQL Database" as DB <<system>>

rectangle "COLORS Web Application" {
  usecase "Log In" as UC_Login
  usecase "Validate Credentials" as UC_Validate
  usecase "Show Login Error" as UC_LoginErr
  usecase "Add Color" as UC_Add
  usecase "Search Colors" as UC_Search
  usecase "Check Session\n(read cookie)" as UC_Session
  usecase "Log Out" as UC_Logout
}

User --> UC_Login
User --> UC_Add
User --> UC_Search
User --> UC_Logout

UC_Login ..> UC_Validate : <<include>>
UC_LoginErr ..> UC_Login : <<extend>>\n[login/password incorrect]
UC_Add ..> UC_Session : <<include>>
UC_Search ..> UC_Session : <<include>>

UC_Validate --> DB
UC_Add --> DB
UC_Search --> DB

note bottom of UC_Session
  color.html calls readCookie() on load;
  if no userId cookie, the user is
  redirected back to index.html.
end note

note top of UC_Login
  Accounts must already exist in the
  Users table (no registration,
  no edit or delete of colors).
end note
@enduml
